# Accepted Trivy findings. Each entry expires, so CI fails again and the decision is revisited.
#
# Spring Framework 6.2.x: these CVEs are only fixed in 7.0.9 (Spring Boot 4). Upgrading to
# Spring Boot 4 is a larger migration and is tracked as known debt.
# The application does not use XSLT views, Server-Sent Events or WebFlux functional endpoints
# directly; WebFlux is on the classpath through Spring AI.
# Accepted 2026-10-21. Review by 2027-01-31 at the latest.

# spring-webmvc: remote code execution via XsltView path handling
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-01-31
# spring-webmvc/spring-webflux: stream corruption in Server-Sent Events with views
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-01-31
# spring-webflux: header predicate bypass in functional endpoints
CVE-2026-47892 exp:2027-01-31
